dayz-server-operator (0.1.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: dzo binary, config.yaml conffile, dayz system
    user via sysusers.d/tmpfiles.d, subuid/subgid + linger setup in
    postinst. No instance management commands ship yet (Phase 1 is
    still in progress); see IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.
  * Player bans with evidence (dzo ban, dzo evidence, web UI, API);
    new dependency modernc.org/sqlite (pure Go, statically linked).
  * Player actions: kick with a reason (BattlEye), heal, fix gear and kill
    (dzo-admin 0.2.0, which changes the packaged PBO), in the API, the CLI
    and the web player panel. New permissions player.kick, player.kill,
    player.heal, player.fixgear.
  * IP addresses are personal data: player.ip (operator) shows the current
    address, ip.history (admin) the stored ones; bans and evidence carry
    opaque references instead. New config keys serve.ip_retention_days
    (default 90) and serve.vacuum_days (default 7); the ban database
    schema gains migration 0002.
  * Country flags in the player list; the player info shows the country,
    and with player.ip the city, approximate location and autonomous
    system. GeoLite2 .mmdb files (geoipupdate, /var/lib/GeoIP) give all of
    it, the legacy GeoIP.dat/GeoIPv6.dat of geoip-database (/usr/share/GeoIP)
    the country only and are the fallback. New dependency
    github.com/oschwald/geoip2-golang/v2 (ISC); new Depends:
    geoip-database, iso-flags-svg; new config keys serve.geoip_dir,
    serve.geoip_legacy_dir and web.flags_dir; new API route
    .../players/{steamid}/geo and a country field in the player list.
  * servermods.lock pins the servermod commits and PBO hashes; CI checks it.
  * The web interface ships a helicopter icon (Font Awesome Free 6.7.2,
    CC BY 4.0) that fonts-fork-awesome lacks; debian/copyright lists it.
  * Message ways: dzo player msg, the API and the web interface send by
    chat colour, on-screen notification, DayZ Expansion notification
    (six types) or RCon say; dzo-admin 0.3.0 (the packaged PBO changes)
    reports Expansion in its hello. New restarts.announce.ways and
    updates.restart_announce.ways: the countdown uses on-screen
    notifications once a minute in the last ten minutes by default, with
    RCon say as the fallback (API token: $DZO_TOKEN or announce.token,
    which dzo instance apply and dzo units sync create with the
    announcer role when an instance runs dzo-admin).
  * Map: territory flags (flag icon, time until the flag goes down) and,
    with DayZ Expansion, territory circles with the territory name, for
    operators; dzo-admin 0.4.0 (the packaged PBO changes). Operators can
    raise a flag from the map (new permission flag.raise, dzo flag raise,
    POST /instances/<i>/flags/<id>/raise).
  * Event feed: dzo-admin 0.5.0 reports kills (Expansion AI too), deaths,
    joins and leaves, base building and raids, flags and stashes; dzo adds
    in-game chat (BattlEye RCon) and admin actions. The newest 1000 events
    per instance are kept in <paths.db>/feed/<instance>.jsonl. GET
    /instances/<i>/feed, stream?only=feed, a live events page with a chat
    input in the web interface, dzo events [-f] on the console, and a Discord
    killfeed (instance.yaml killfeed, with an optional delay for PvP servers;
    Discord posts no longer ping anyone). The notifier gets a 10 second HTTP
    timeout.
  * Web interface: an instance switcher and an instance bar on every page,
    world, time, uptime, restart and mod version on the dashboard, a fixed
    teleport drag on the map, and a player database (Players page, API
    /players, permission player.history) with BattlEye global bans (asked
    from BattlEye's master server, per game) and Steam bans (optional Web API
    key, steam.web_api_key_file). New options steam.profile_lookup,
    steam.web_api_key_file and serve.session_retention_days.
  * Map: rebuilt houses and wells with the time until decay wears them down,
    the tunnel entrances (with and without a usable rope ladder) and an active
    sandstorm; dzo-admin 0.6.1 (the packaged PBO changes).
  * Killfeed: an Expansion AI is shown with its own name and its faction,
    AI "Frida" (West); the faction is no longer a raw stringtable key.
  * Move vehicles (drag on the map, "Move to coordinates", dzo vehicle move,
    POST /vehicles/<id>/move) to pull stuck ones out. A vehicle with players
    inside moves at most admin.move_occupied_max metres (new option, default
    200) and everyone takes no damage for 3 s; dzo-admin 0.7.0 (the packaged
    PBO changes).
  * Boats (vanilla and DayZ Expansion) are listed on the map and in the vehicle
    list as kind boat and can be spawned on the water, repaired, flipped, moved
    and deleted like cars; dzo-admin 0.7.0.

 -- Bernd Zeimetz <bernd@bzed.de>  Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0000
